WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.412
Today we have something
a little different.

00:00:03.412 --> 00:00:07.412
Dr. Jane Goodall 
is going to tell you a story.

00:00:07.418 --> 00:00:09.308
Stay tuned after
the animation

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:12.378
to learn how to download
this as a free children's book.

00:00:13.308 --> 00:00:15.038
Ready?

00:00:15.038 --> 00:00:16.257
Let's begin.

00:00:20.425 --> 00:00:23.205
It starts as a whisper,

00:00:23.205 --> 00:00:25.352
a word on the air.

00:00:25.352 --> 00:00:29.182
It can't quite be heard,
but you know that it's there.

00:00:30.452 --> 00:00:32.562
As gentle
as sunlight,

00:00:32.562 --> 00:00:34.362
as tenacious
as hale,

00:00:34.362 --> 00:00:38.102
in its route to the heart,
it could not but prevail.

00:00:39.292 --> 00:00:42.872
And the people looked up
from their day-to-day tasks,

00:00:42.872 --> 00:00:44.922
their day-to-day jobs

00:00:44.922 --> 00:00:47.064
and their 
day-to-day masks.

00:00:47.972 --> 00:00:50.332
They heard 
or they felt

00:00:50.332 --> 00:00:51.972
where the whisper
could lead,

00:00:51.972 --> 00:00:54.352
and they looked 
with eyes wide

00:00:54.352 --> 00:00:57.352
at what that
might mean.

00:00:57.352 --> 00:01:01.623
And once they could see it,
they hadn't a chance

00:01:01.623 --> 00:01:04.253
To resist the 
sweet song

00:01:04.253 --> 00:01:06.413
of the deep spell
it cast.

00:01:08.383 --> 00:01:11.533
But the feeling it brought 
them at first glance

00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:13.073
was pain,

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:17.453
as they lifted their eyes
on the land they had claimed.

00:01:17.453 --> 00:01:19.393
Since they saw
at last

00:01:19.393 --> 00:01:21.613
as if raised
from a dream,

00:01:22.983 --> 00:01:26.513
they were almost alone
on the land and the sea.

00:01:29.598 --> 00:01:31.858
For the trees 
had almost gone,

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.208
and the bees
had almost gone,

00:01:34.208 --> 00:01:36.858
and the creatures
in their shells by the seas

00:01:36.858 --> 00:01:38.428
had almost gone.

00:01:38.428 --> 00:01:41.948
And the people felt sad
as they saw their new Earth,

00:01:41.948 --> 00:01:44.268
but they knew 
this was it,

00:01:44.268 --> 00:01:47.338
one wild chance 
for rebirth.

00:01:49.491 --> 00:01:53.001
Breaking new ground,
seeds rolling down,

00:01:53.001 --> 00:01:56.921
smell of the earth on 
your hands and your brow.

00:01:56.921 --> 00:02:01.221
No time for sorrow,
we're building tomorrow.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:05.271
The sound of things growing
now keeps us around.

00:02:07.469 --> 00:02:11.469
As the wildness grows,
and the deep wood grows,

00:02:11.469 --> 00:02:14.120
and the sense that the
future's come to meet you

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:15.800
grows,

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.110
There's no chance
we can rest.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.620
We must do 
our best.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.220
This moment can lead
us back home,

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.000
that's our test.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.860
It starts as 
a whisper,

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.420
a word on 
the air.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:36.285
It can't quite be heard,
but you know that it's there.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.790
It then spoke
like thunder.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.620
Until we all moved.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:43.920
And we could.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.230
And we did.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:46.505
And it's done.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.259
She's renewed.

00:02:54.872 --> 00:03:00.622
Help turn the whisper into a roar 
by sharing this poem today.

00:03:00.622 --> 00:03:07.171
You can download the illustrated book 
for free at ed.ted.com/whisper

00:03:07.171 --> 00:03:11.871
or keep your soul aflutter with one 
of these animated poems.

